---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
const interests = ['Software engineering', 'AI coding agents', 'Local models', 'Automation', 'Developer tools', 'Indie games'];
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="Meet Isaac, the software engineer behind After Bedtime Labs. A personal workshop for software, AI, developer tools, and games built outside the day job.">
  <div class="container about-page">
    <header class="about-header"><p class="eyebrow">A little context</p><h1 class="page-heading">Engineer by day.<br /><em>Curious after hours.</em></h1><p class="page-intro">I’m Isaac. A husband, dad, and software engineer who likes making things and understanding how they work.</p></header>
    <div class="about-body">
      <aside class="about-aside"><span class="about-mark" aria-hidden="true"><Icon name="lamp" size={66} /></span><p class="eyebrow">After Bedtime Labs</p><p>Small windows of time.<br />Room to experiment.</p></aside>
      <div class="about-copy prose"><h2>The hours in between</h2><p>I’ve spent roughly a decade working professionally in software engineering. Outside work, my priorities are my family. The projects here happen in the available time after the day job and bedtime.</p><p>That’s where the name comes from. After Bedtime Labs is my personal workshop: a home for the software I build, the experiments I try, and the things I learn.</p><h2>What draws me in</h2><p>I’m interested in tools that make development more useful and enjoyable, from AI coding agents and local language models to desktop utilities and automation. I also like the different kind of problem solving that comes with building games.</p><div class="interests">{interests.map(interest => <span class="tag">{interest}</span>)}</div><h2>Notes, with the rough edges left in</h2><p>The goal is to document what actually works, what doesn’t, and what changes my understanding along the way. An unfinished experiment can still teach something useful. I want the writing here to reflect that.</p><p>If you’re here to get a sense of how I think and build, the <a href="/projects/">projects</a> and <a href="/writing/">writing</a> are a good place to start.</p><div class="about-social"><a class="text-link" href={site.github}>GitHub <Icon name="arrow-up-right" size={16} /></a><a class="text-link" href={site.x}>@AfterBedtimeDev on X <Icon name="arrow-up-right" size={16} /></a>{site.linkedin && <a class="text-link" href={site.linkedin}>LinkedIn <Icon name="arrow-up-right" size={16} /></a>}</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .about-page { padding-top: 65px; } .about-header { padding-bottom: 52px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); } h1 em { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-weight: 400; color: var(--accent); } .about-header .page-intro { max-width: 570px; }
  .about-body { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 2.1fr; gap: 85px; padding-top: 46px; } .about-aside { padding-top: 20px; } .about-mark { display: inline-grid; place-items: center; width: 112px; height: 112px; background: var(--surface); border-radius: 50%; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 27px; } .about-aside > p:last-child { font-size: 14px; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 13px; }
  .about-copy { max-width: 680px; font-size: 17px; } .about-copy h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; } .about-copy h2 { font-size: 27px; margin-top: 1.9em; } .about-copy p { color: var(--muted); } .interests { display: flex; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; } .about-social { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 25px; padding-top: 18px; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .about-page { padding-top: 44px; } .about-body { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 30px; padding-top: 34px; } .about-aside { display: none; } .about-header { padding-bottom: 35px; } }
</style>
